name pyluatex
category Package
revision 63491
shortdesc Execute Python code on the fly in your LaTeX documents
longdesc PyLuaTeX allows you to execute Python code and to include the
longdesc resulting output in your LaTeX documents in a single
longdesc compilation run. LaTeX documents must be compiled with LuaLaTeX
longdesc for this to work. PyLuaTeX runs a Python InteractiveInterpreter
longdesc (actually several if you use different sessions) in the
longdesc background for on-the-fly code execution. Python code from your
longdesc LaTeX file is sent to the background interpreter through a TCP
longdesc socket. This approach allows your Python code to be executed
longdesc and the output to be integrated in your LaTeX file in a single
longdesc compilation run. No additional processing steps are needed. No
longdesc intermediate files have to be written. No placeholders have to
longdesc be inserted.
